{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance","id":1248119,"title":"Will Lunars have clear ways to keep the spirit shape of central importance?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-20T10:09:27-07:00","id":1248119,"title":"Will Lunars have clear ways to keep the spirit shape of central importance?","content":"An issue that plagued earlier editions of Ars Magica was that the wizards who were given by their house upbringing the ability to change into their &quot;heartbeast&quot;, an animal form that was tied to their nature, didn't have any way to mechanically expand that ability. They could learn to turn into other things, but they didn't have anything unique that they could do with their personal animal. So, baring a lot of effort on the part of the player to stick to theme, the more that they studied, the less connected to their heartbeast they became. The characters were more or less forced to develop in ways that were contrary to their original theme.<br /> <br /> It strikes me that Lunars could have a similar issue. It could be that the more that they gain abilities the less of a focus their spirit shape becomes. Do we know if there are ways to mechanically develop their spirit shape? Would a player have the option to, as their character acquires more xp, make the spirit shape a bigger deal rather than just a starting point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T10:13:56-07:00","id":1248121,"title":"","content":"Native Lunar Attribute Charms are how I go from being a tiger to an Exalted tiger who is super strong, tough, fast, graceful, and also 50 feet long from nose to tail while still able to sneak around like a mouse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T10:19:10-07:00","id":1248125,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure their hybrid form (and thus Deadly Beastman form) needs to be based upon their spirit shape. <br /> <br /> So if you're spirit shape is a tiger you need to be a tiger-person, and if it's a fish you need to be a fish person. <br /> <br /> Oh, also we know that lunar charms will sometimes have the &quot;totemic&quot; keyword, which can give you alternate prerequisites on certain charms if you have a certain spirit shape. Usually for an attribute that fits that animal better than the standard prerequisite does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T10:37:20-07:00","id":1248129,"title":"","content":"I feel as though the Totemic keyword and the hybrid body are something that will persistently give spirit shape a visual prominence, but I can't really think of a way for the shape itself to be continuously developed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T10:58:51-07:00","id":1248137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248129#post1248129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the Totemic keyword and the hybrid body are something that will persistently give spirit shape a visual prominence, but I can't really think of a way for the shape itself to be continuously developed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can spend XP to learn any Latent Abilities, but not any Magical ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T11:32:52-07:00","id":1248150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248125#post1248125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if you're spirit shape is a tiger you need to be a tiger-person, and if it's a fish you need to be a fish person.</div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>get</i> to be a fish person. and then you can learn <a href=\"https://youtu.be/37zPuwz5s58?t=27\" target=\"_blank\">Fishman Karate</a>. All of the awesome, practically none of the Dagon*!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>*Dagon will rise. Dagon is the shadow in the water. Dagon is the blood of the old. Dagon. Dagon. </i></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T11:33:38-07:00","id":1248152,"title":"","content":"I think in practice it's more &quot;magical abilities are called charms&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T21:46:20-07:00","id":1248315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248129#post1248129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though the Totemic keyword and the hybrid body are something that will persistently give spirit shape a visual prominence, but I can't really think of a way for the shape itself to be continuously developed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could imagine Lunars having the potential for getting charms that boost animal shapes, much like Solar Survival charms, but unless those are restricted to being used in your Totem form, it doesn\u2019t seem like that would necessarily help your Totem shape retain prominence. <br /> <br /> Though, I suppose a combination of mote cost discounts and bonuses if using it in Totem shape could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T23:13:39-07:00","id":1248334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248315#post1248315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could imagine Lunars having the potential for getting charms that boost animal shapes, much like Solar Survival charms, but unless those are restricted to being used in your Totem form, it doesn\u2019t seem like that would necessarily help your Totem shape retain prominence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Previews have revealed that the <b>Protean </b>keyword will grant bennies when <i>in </i>appropriate animal shapes while the <b>Totemic </b>keyword allows the charm to be learned with an alternate ability if you <i>have </i>the appropriate spirit shape. Different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 08-21-2018, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T01:23:06-07:00","id":1248351,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we've known about the Protean keyword for... ages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248137#post1248137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can spend XP to learn any Latent Abilities, but not any Magical ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that something they'll be able to do with all of their animal shapes, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T02:43:51-07:00","id":1248365,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but a combination of protean and totemic (if there are any charms with both keywords) will lend itself to a greater focus on charms that are boosted in one's spirit shape, encouraging its use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T03:18:32-07:00","id":1248370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248365#post1248365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but a combination of protean and totemic (if there are any charms with both keywords) will lend itself to a greater focus on charms that are boosted in one's spirit shape, encouraging its use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so...<br /> <br /> A Protean Charm with the Totemic Keyword will stand out as one that resonates immediately with the spirit shape of a Lunar that can benefit from the alternative Attribute. If you have your choice of Wits or Stamina for Adder and Toad Method, then you'll definitely be somebody who can benefit from its Protean aspects, as opposed to having to go out of your way to get a shape to get the benefits of, say, Octopus and Spider Barrage.<br /> <br /> \u2026Okay, that's a bad example, since a lot of animals with more than four limbs (such as both of the ones in the Charm's name) are also actually venomous, but you get my point.<br /> <br /> And the Totemic keyword will benefit people not having their build hamstrung by things that would make sense for their concept.<br /> <br /> However... assuming a Lunar that favours either Stamina or Wits has a venomous spirit shape, but also has, say, ten other animal forms at character creation, their use of that poison Charm is no more benefited than any Protean Charms that would go with any of their other shapes. At least not with the information that we have right now.<br /> <br /> Indeed, considering that the effect of the Totemic keyword is based on diversifying Attributes, that may actually encourage having Protean Charms to benefit forms other than your spirit shape. Being able to focus on Wits means that you have an easier time accessing any Protean Charms in Wits, that may go far afield from your poisonous totem. <br /> <br /> But the main thing is that the combination of Protean and Totemic does not currently appear to be something that makes the spirit shape any more useful than any other.<br /> <br /> On the face of it, I think that's a good thing; the spirit shape is not irrelevant for the manner in which it might inform one's Tell, one's Anima banner and the mutations one can get in the hybrid body, but it would also not be a thing that constrains the image of Lunars as increasingly diverse shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> I did, however, think of something else that might give spirit shape a bit of emphasis; if there are still significant things in Lunar mechanics that draw distinctions based on being in a &quot;true&quot; form, and if the spirit shape will still count as one of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T09:12:31-07:00","id":1248426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248334#post1248334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Previews have revealed that the <b>Protean </b>keyword will grant bennies when <i>in </i>appropriate animal shapes while the <b>Totemic </b>keyword allows the charm to be learned with an alternate ability if you <i>have </i>the appropriate spirit shape. Different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but Protean seems like the Lunar equivalent of those Aura charms that give you an extra benefit while in a particular aura. I\u2019m talking about charms where the entire point is boosting your animal form. If they build those so they cost fewer motes if you\u2019re in Totem form, then that could provide an incentive to use it, without being too restrictive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T09:14:25-07:00","id":1248427,"title":"","content":"We do not want to mechanically reward Lunars for choosing particular totems. No more encouraging Lunars to have either tyrant lizards or flying birds for their spirit shapes because those are mechanically optimal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T09:28:04-07:00","id":1248430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248427#post1248427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We do not want to mechanically reward Lunars for choosing particular totems. No more encouraging Lunars to have either tyrant lizards or flying birds for their spirit shapes because those are mechanically optimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Totemic charms are far enough. The ability to snipe charm trees out of attribute due to your spirit shape is pretty potent.<br /> <br /> It does incentivize spirits shapes somewhat but only in such a way as to encourage character concepts which I think is not a bad way to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T09:41:20-07:00","id":1248436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248426#post1248426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I\u2019m talking about charms where the entire point is boosting your animal form.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hmm, that doesn't really feel right to me. Not for any elaborate reason, just... it feels off.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I suppose one question would be if they're Charms tied to specific categories, or just generically boost a kind of animal.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Although for the latter... maybe if there were some kind of shapeshifting Charms that provide enhancements specifically to your spirit shape, although that still feels like something exclusive.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Unless... is this counting things like letting animal forms be of unusual size? Maybe my opposition is just faulty at the roots...</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248427#post1248427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We do not want to mechanically reward Lunars for choosing particular totems. No more encouraging Lunars to have either tyrant lizards or flying birds for their spirit shapes because those are mechanically optimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though that ship has kind of sailed if there's going to be a whole class of Charms exclusive to chimeras, and no drawbacks to being one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T11:10:17-07:00","id":1248465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248430#post1248430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Totemic charms are far enough. The ability to snipe charm trees out of attribute due to your spirit shape is pretty potent.<br /> <br /> It does incentivize spirits shapes somewhat but only in such a way as to encourage character concepts which I think is not a bad way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. ( char limit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T11:28:34-07:00","id":1248473,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the problem with the old rules was they incentivised powerful totems over characterful totems. The totemic keyword makes your character's powers more thematic.<br /> <br /> I think, in the new rules, there probably isn't much incentive to fight in your true form*, but I can't see an easy way to solve that doesn't lead back to people picking power totems.<br /> <br /> *Saying this, if your totems is, say, a bear, then at character gen you've got a free bear form. Fighting as a Tyrant Lizard might be better, but doing the sacred hunt on a tyrant lizard really isn't easy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T11:38:40-07:00","id":1248475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248365#post1248365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but a combination of protean and totemic (if there are any charms with both keywords) will lend itself to a greater focus on charms that are boosted in one's spirit shape, encouraging its use.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly the sort of thing that I was hoping to see, (hopefully it will work in play).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T12:59:19-07:00","id":1248488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248475#post1248475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly the sort of thing that I was hoping to see</div> </div> </div> </div>You're seeing the discussion following that post, right?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T13:01:05-07:00","id":1248490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248473#post1248473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the problem with the old rules was they incentivised powerful totems over characterful totems. The totemic keyword makes your character's powers more thematic.<br /> <br /> I think, in the new rules, there probably isn't much incentive to fight in your true form*, but I can't see an easy way to solve that doesn't lead back to people picking power totems.<br /> <br /> *Saying this, if your totems is, say, a bear, then at character gen you've got a free bear form. Fighting as a Tyrant Lizard might be better, but doing the sacred hunt on a tyrant lizard really isn't easy!</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s probably easier if you use Mountainous Spirit Expression, which requires the Towering Beast Shape Charm you would need in the first place for turning into a tyrant lizard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T13:35:47-07:00","id":1248498,"title":"","content":"Isn't that a higher essence charm anyway, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T14:31:59-07:00","id":1248519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248498#post1248498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that a higher essence charm anyway, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Towering Beast Shape would need to be Essence 1 for Lunars with super-sized spirit shapes. This is supposed to be balanced by the Charm\u2019s crushing costs.<br /> <br /> Mountainous Spirit Expression is hardly an expansion on that Charm\u2019s power, unless you count the ability to use Martial Arts and warstrider-scaled versions of your moonsilver armor and weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T01:03:04-07:00","id":1248654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248436#post1248436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I feel as though that ship has kind of sailed if there's going to be a whole class of Charms exclusive to chimeras, and no drawbacks to being one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there? My read on Chimeras was they were mostly &quot;you get more totem charms&quot;. Especially since I understood you only being able to hybrid 2 totems, not add 3+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T01:13:57-07:00","id":1248655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248654#post1248654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there? My read on Chimeras was they were mostly &quot;you get more totem charms&quot;. Especially since I understood you only being able to hybrid 2 totems, not add 3+.</div> </div> </div> </div>You were mistaken; developers and playtesters have made it clear that there is an actual cascade of chimera themed Charms that are gated behind the Charm that allows you to become a chimera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T01:45:56-07:00","id":1248657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248655#post1248655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You were mistaken; developers and playtesters have made it clear that there is an actual cascade of chimera themed Charms that are gated behind the Charm that allows you to become a chimera.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, thank you for the clarification!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T02:32:34-07:00","id":1248662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248427#post1248427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We do not want to mechanically reward Lunars for choosing particular totems. No more encouraging Lunars to have either tyrant lizards or flying birds for their spirit shapes because those are mechanically optimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm.<br /> <br /> I used to agree with this line of thinking, but after turning it over in my head a lot, here's my problem with that. If your spirit shape isn't mechanically <i>meaningful</i>, players are going to sense this and it will affect the feel of the game. Yes, not everything needs to be mechanically meaningful - it's not like your hair color... well, ok, that does matter sometimes.<br /> <br /> But I think that your spirit shape is something that <i>feels</i> like it should be mechanically meaningful. &quot;I bear the soul of a mighty bear!&quot; should be different from &quot;I bear the soul of a nimble gazelle!&quot;, and making it so either one can just trivially grab the other form and then they play 99% identically as characters takes away from that.<br /> <br /> And given the broad number of possible forms, if they're going to be mechanically distinct as spirit shapes... it's not going to be reasonably possible to balance all of them. So the alternative is &quot;make them all play similarly, and accept that your spirit shape is not a very mechanically important choice&quot; or &quot;make them all play differently, in ways that avoid <i>overt</i> balance issues between them, and just trust players to work out the rest.&quot;<br /> <br /> Between those two options I think I prefer the latter - I'll always go for a more interesting game over a more balanced one. If you're willing to sacrifice interesting gameplay for balance, what's even the point of your game, anyway?<br /> <br /> Obviously some forms will be more broadly useful to be <i>in</i>, so I think that rather than making the inherent spirit shape benefits too strong, what I'd prefer to do is emphasize the significance of your spirit shape by letting you create unique evocation-style powers based on it (ones that are only possible for Lunars with that spirit shape or one similar to it.) Some shapes are obviously going to have more room for these than others, but since they cost XP, and since each individual purchase should be worth roughly the same amount, the potential balance issues are much less extreme - if you choose a spirit form that doesn't lend itself well to combat powers, well, that's a statement you made about your character; but you can still spend that XP elsewhere.<br /> <br /> They wouldn't actually be evocations, though. I'd make them cost actual charm XP to further avoid punishing people who take a narrow spirit shape.<br /> <br /> Oh, another thing they could be used for is &quot;evolving&quot; your Spirit Shape - upgrading it to a more powerful thematically-related form that Lunars couldn't take as a Spirit Shape at chargen. So your bird can become a phoenix, your lizard can become a dragon, your Magikarp becomes a Gyarados and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 08-22-2018, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T07:47:25-07:00","id":1248706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248662#post1248662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> <br /> Oh, another thing they could be used for is &quot;evolving&quot; your Spirit Shape - upgrading it to a more powerful thematically-related form that Lunars couldn't take as a Spirit Shape at chargen. So your bird can become a phoenix, your lizard can become a dragon, your Magikarp becomes a Gyarados and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars having pocket monster familiars is already approaching &quot;on the nose&quot; for Pokemon; &quot;upgrading&quot; your spirit shape seems like it would shift to being dead-on for a reference and give the wrong impression, especially when the Lunar's spirit shape is already legendary, because it is associated with the Lunar. At least, unless you're going for a straight-up daikaijuu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T07:54:53-07:00","id":1248708,"title":"","content":"You turn your bird into a phoenix by eating fire elementals and stealing their eclipse charms, generally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T08:35:05-07:00","id":1248719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248708#post1248708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You turn your bird into a phoenix by eating fire elementals and stealing their eclipse charms, generally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that count? You can presumably still use the Eclipse Charms in other forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T08:47:16-07:00","id":1248721,"title":"","content":"You just gotta come at it with the right attitude. It's your legend. Do it right, and when you turn into a bear people will go &quot;oh, no, the phoenix has transformed into a bear&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T09:00:38-07:00","id":1248725,"title":"","content":"It doesn't even make sense to 'evolve' your spirit shape in this way. <br /> <br /> Currently we have a spirit shape + shapes you pick up with heart's blood + charms.<br /> <br /> Totemic charms are based on spirit shape. If you change your spirit shape, do you lose access to your totemic charms? If you want to pick up a phoenix form, why would you want to <i>lose</i> access to your bird spirit shape? You can have <i>both</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T10:47:45-07:00","id":1248745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248721#post1248721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just gotta come at it with the right attitude. It's your legend. Do it right, and when you turn into a bear people will go &quot;oh, no, the phoenix has transformed into a bear&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, a Lunar capacity to get Eclipse Charms still strikes me as more of a parallel to various characters from WW's Werewolf games learning Gifts. Secondly, we don't need another edition of treating animal forms as a stepping stone to &quot;greater things&quot; that's to be abandoned the moment you reach a certain Essence rating. Especially since it was explicitly supposed to give good reasons for using animal forms, built right into the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T18:54:59-07:00","id":1248805,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what that has to do with what I said. I meant that the &quot;phoenix form&quot; would just be their regular bird form with added fire elemental charms, and if they got a rep as said phoenix that's what everyone would think of them as regardless of what form they took.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T19:42:18-07:00","id":1248810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248805#post1248805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what that has to do with what I said. I meant that the &quot;phoenix form&quot; would just be their regular bird form with added fire elemental charms, and if they got a rep as said phoenix that's what everyone would think of them as regardless of what form they took.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lore problem: &quot;phoenix&quot; refers to a specific form of the garda birds, which is humanoid, with six arms and an eagle's head. So, the term &quot;phoenix&quot; as commonly used in Creation is going to have different baggage. You can try to look like some other avian fire elemental, but it seems like it'd be far more reliable to be the eagle that stole the heart of a flame and wields it as a weapon. Not a god, not a demon, but a beast of legend that transcends what others think of beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-23T03:00:43-07:00","id":1248827,"title":"","content":"*shrug* I guess. Creation's probably big enough to fit at least one non-garda bird phoenix though. It manages two sorts of dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-23T05:50:44-07:00","id":1248846,"title":"","content":"While I still like the idea of being able to play a dragon-totem Lunar, I appreciate the equality that means Heaven, Hell, and the Realm could all be made to fear Ratatoskr the Squirrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-23T16:16:11-07:00","id":1248866,"title":"","content":"Did the forums break for anyone else, all day today?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T10:23:47-07:00","id":1248874,"title":"","content":"Yeah, for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T12:24:54-07:00","id":1248879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248706#post1248706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars having pocket monster familiars is already approaching &quot;on the nose&quot; for Pokemon; &quot;upgrading&quot; your spirit shape seems like it would shift to being dead-on for a reference and give the wrong impression, especially when the Lunar's spirit shape is already legendary, because it is associated with the Lunar. At least, unless you're going for a straight-up daikaijuu.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty common in the genre, though (xianxia / xuanhuan) for characters who have an animal form or power-source to change along those lines when upgrading. It wouldn't be appropriate for everyone, only for ones that have a clear upgrade path that retains and adds to the thematics of the original (or at least those thematics that have become relevant.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-13-2019, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T12:29:51-07:00","id":1248880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248725#post1248725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totemic charms are based on spirit shape. If you change your spirit shape, do you lose access to your totemic charms? If you want to pick up a phoenix form, why would you want to <i>lose</i> access to your bird spirit shape? You can have <i>both</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your totemic charms might change slightly, but generally finding a form that preserves the important beats of anything you've established already about your character would be a prerequisite to this. If it feels like you're losing something, you're doing it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T21:27:48-07:00","id":1248921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248879#post1248879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty common in the genre, though (xianxia / xuanhuan) for characters who have an animal form or power-source to change along those lines when upgrading. It wouldn't be appropriate for everyone, only for ones that have a clear upgrade path that retains and adds to the thematics of the original (or at least those thematics that have become relevant.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted made a lot of dips into other pools, especially when it comes to Lunars. The most outstanding example of a character type in Exalted that does follow that kind of upgrade progression... is the Alchemicals. Given the wide gap between the Alchemicals and Lunars in thematics (particularly with regard to how the former are utterly reliant on infrastructure while the latter cut all reliance on it away if they ever had any to begin with), I wouldn't expect Lunars to function in that fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T03:18:41-07:00","id":1248935,"title":"","content":"Familiar charms that wok better on familiars that match your spirit shape seem in-keeping with lunars' themes. <br /> <br /> Or, hey, maybe something that works on familiars <i>or</i> members of your spirit shape species. So you can have a lion lunar buffing a pack of lions. Like, &quot;king of the x&quot; type thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T10:41:39-07:00","id":1248977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248657#post1248657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, thank you for the clarification!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, wow; that was not the response that I was expecting.<br /> <br /> I, in fact, was the mistaken one, as Vance clarified that there are not currently any Charms that follow the chimera one when I asked him. I want to say that my information was outdated, unless it was a simple matter of my having always misread statements around the idea of a chimera Charm or Charms. <br /> <br /> That's actually perfectly good for me, because the idea of there being a special class of chimera Charms was something that I accepted, but not something that I liked; it struck me as inevitably making the chimera a superior form of Lunar, by virtue of having access to the most Charms.<br /> <br /> Hence, my comment on the departed ship of superior spirit shapes has also been rendered invalid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T10:42:35-07:00","id":1248978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1248657#post1248657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh, thank you for the clarification!</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh, wow; that was not the response that I was expecting.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I, in fact, was the mistaken one, as Vance clarified that there are not currently any Charms that follow the chimera one when I asked him. I want to say that my information was outdated, unless it was a simple matter of my having always misread statements around the idea of a chimera Charm or Charms. </span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's actually perfectly good for me, because the idea of there being a special class of chimera Charms was something that I accepted, but not something that I liked; it struck me as inevitably making the chimera a superior form of Lunar, by virtue of having access to the most Charms.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hence, my comment on the departed ship of superior spirit shapes has also been rendered invalid.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T15:47:12-07:00","id":1249024,"title":"","content":"Testing, testing. How's the forum working, now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T16:57:25-07:00","id":1249035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249024#post1249024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Testing, testing. How's the forum working, now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quirky. When I made my response a few posts up, I got an &quot;empty post&quot; notification, but in cutting the text, pasting it back, and trying to post again to see if that did anything, got a message that the forum requires posters to wait before making new posts, so I canceled the message, reloaded, and saw my reply as I had typed it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T02:21:02-07:00","id":1249082,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I got the Empty post but it still appeared when I reloaded. And yesterday morning it didn't work on my phone, but did on my PC, and then it worked on my phone again.<br /> <br /> I think it's mostly okay, but not 100%. I notice people haven't posted much, maybe others have been having problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T03:30:39-07:00","id":1249089,"title":"","content":"So, on the subject of Lunars giving prominence to spirit shape by means of iteratively enhancing it, I wouldn't really be for it. Not even primarily for the concern of treating animal shapes as a baby step that they ultimately outgrow; mostly because I see mundanity in the shapes of even old and powerful Lunars as being part of the Charm.<br /> <br /> \u2026.Of the <i>charm</i>. Damn muscle memory.<br /> <br /> I keep thinking about how leaning too heavily into the spirit shape is kind of putting Lunars at risk of becoming a collection of animal Exigents, and even if that's a far extreme... I don't know, the idea of it being <i>very</i> important is something that has never quite sat right with me, just because it's generally something that one chooses at the start and sticks with. I think that the spirit shape should matter, but matter a lot less than generally being a Lunar, with the Charms in common and the capacity to develop a library of shapes.<br /> <br /> In that sense, it's a lot like anima banner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T05:25:45-07:00","id":1249099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249089#post1249089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, on the subject of Lunars giving prominence to spirit shape by means of iteratively enhancing it, I wouldn't really be for it. Not even primarily for the concern of treating animal shapes as a baby step that they ultimately outgrow; mostly because I see mundanity in the shapes of even old and powerful Lunars as being part of the Charm.<br /> <br /> \u2026.Of the <i>charm</i>. Damn muscle memory.<br /> <br /> I keep thinking about how leaning too heavily into the spirit shape is kind of putting Lunars at risk of becoming a collection of animal Exigents, and even if that's a far extreme... I don't know, the idea of it being <i>very</i> important is something that has never quite sat right with me, just because it's generally something that one chooses at the start and sticks with. I think that the spirit shape should matter, but matter a lot less than generally being a Lunar, with the Charms in common and the capacity to develop a library of shapes.<br /> <br /> In that sense, it's a lot like anima banner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. At the end of the day, how much do &quot;bats&quot; really define Batman, or &quot;spiders&quot; define Spider-Man?<br /> <br /> For that matter, Sun Wukong is unmistakably a monkey, but that doesn't limit what he can turn into, and his greatest combat feats that I know about don't really have anything to do with fighting as a monkey, but with the magical tricks that he could perform regardless of form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T06:00:06-07:00","id":1249101,"title":"","content":"In terms of giving shapes a particular role through particular Charm paths, my immediate response is to wonder about how that constricts choice of totems. If we go &quot;Oh, a bear totem is strong, hardy, slow moving, and you get Charms that follow that path&quot;, then how do you deal with a person who wants to choose a nimble, tree climbing spectacled bear as their totem? One choice is to say &quot;That person is a corner case who can just reskin the paths allowed for a monkey totem&quot; but then that somewhat undermines the feel that are you are trying to create - that totems are *real* with *real* effects that are specific to *that* totem alone - in making Charm paths totem dependent. This is even if you do see that as the desirable goal and discount heavily on the potential Isator raises for them to feel like animal avatar Exigents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T06:42:59-07:00","id":1249113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249099#post1249099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. At the end of the day, how much do &quot;bats&quot; really define Batman, or &quot;spiders&quot; define Spider-Man?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends; is the latter being written by J Michael Straczynski at the time?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, Sun Wukong is unmistakably a monkey, but that doesn't limit what he can turn into, and his greatest combat feats that I know about don't really have anything to do with fighting as a monkey, but with the magical tricks that he could perform regardless of form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually argued against looking to Sun Wukong as an inspiration for things that Lunars can do in the past, but I'd say in his own story and as a guideline for Lunars there is something to the idea of him conveying a kind of monkey attitude in his actions and motives.<br /> <br /> I'm suddenly thinking of an approach to totems that is somewhat like treating them as an underlayer to Caste, in terms of developing personality and method. Helped by how the Lunar Castes are a lot more bare bones than the others, or even than Terrestrial Aspects. It would be subtle, but I'd say it can be the kind of thing that gives the spirit shape prominence no matter how far the powers are developed; that the true, original, core you is a person who first turned into X animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T06:55:49-07:00","id":1249118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249101#post1249101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of giving shapes a particular role through particular Charm paths, my immediate response is to wonder about how that constricts choice of totems. If we go &quot;Oh, a bear totem is strong, hardy, slow moving, and you get Charms that follow that path&quot;, then how do you deal with a person who wants to choose a nimble, tree climbing spectacled bear as their totem? One choice is to say &quot;That person is a corner case who can just reskin the paths allowed for a monkey totem&quot; but then that somewhat undermines the feel that are you are trying to create - that totems are *real* with *real* effects that are specific to *that* totem alone - in making Charm paths totem dependent. This is even if you do see that as the desirable goal and discount heavily on the potential Isator raises for them to feel like animal avatar Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why your totem beast is your totem beast has always been a self-defined thing. It's not like Shadowrun, where they give you a list of pre-defined totems and you have to choose.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T07:10:24-07:00","id":1249122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249101#post1249101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of giving shapes a particular role through particular Charm paths, my immediate response is to wonder about how that constricts choice of totems. If we go &quot;Oh, a bear totem is strong, hardy, slow moving, and you get Charms that follow that path&quot;, then how do you deal with a person who wants to choose a nimble, tree climbing spectacled bear as their totem? One choice is to say &quot;That person is a corner case who can just reskin the paths allowed for a monkey totem&quot; but then that somewhat undermines the feel that are you are trying to create - that totems are *real* with *real* effects that are specific to *that* totem alone - in making Charm paths totem dependent. This is even if you do see that as the desirable goal and discount heavily on the potential Isator raises for them to feel like animal avatar Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the key is that the Totem adds <i>extra</i> favoured charms. But you're still getting your Caste and Favoured charms. I guess that's a bit similar to what Isator said above, it's like an extra caste.<br /> <br /> So, if your totem is a fringe case, well, you can still Favour Dexterity because you think it fits your character, and thus all Dex charms are favoured.<br /> <br /> I also don't think that, generally speaking, Totem charms are going to be things like &quot;if your totem is a burly buff bear you get this Soak-boosting charm as a Wits charm.&quot; That doesn't make much sense.<br /> <br /> Rather, I think it's more stuff that's particularly animal-esque.<br /> For example, the poison charms are Stamina charms with the Totem keyword. If your totem is poisonous or toxic, you can take them (well, some at least, I don't know if it's all of them) as Wits charms.<br /> <br /> So, if you're playing Serpentor the evil No Moon snake-sorcerer (who, of course, lives in a giant snake-keep with his army of snake-men), the fact that you don't favour Stamina doesn't stop you taking a bunch of poison charms. <br /> <br /> Things like charms that are just about being really strong or really tough, I don't expect to have the Totem keyword. I think it'll be the more animal-themed ones, to ensure you can take charms that iconically fit the animal even if the normal Favoured attribute doesn't fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T07:45:38-07:00","id":1249134,"title":"","content":"Perhaps this can answer some of folks' questions:<br /> <br /> I have avoided anything that might make your choice of spirit shape a point of character optimization as a very conscious decision. Yes, it unlocks new possibilities through the Totemic keyword, but those are still Charms you could've gotten the normal way; it just opens up alternative paths. I don't want people to be discouraged from picking &quot;suboptimal&quot; spirit shapes that fit their character concepts, and I especially don't want to see the same small selection of animals getting used over and over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T08:02:23-07:00","id":1249138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249122#post1249122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if you're playing Serpentor the evil No Moon snake-sorcerer (who, of course, lives in a giant snake-keep with his army of snake-men), the fact that you don't favour Stamina doesn't stop you taking a bunch of poison charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well he needs the Charisma to make a battle cry of &quot;Cobra-la-la-la!&quot; anything other than silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T10:33:17-07:00","id":1249167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249138#post1249138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well he needs the Charisma to make a battle cry of &quot;Cobra-la-la-la!&quot; anything other than silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't enough Charisma in the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T10:34:19-07:00","id":1249169,"title":"","content":"Rephrasing my original post so that it's more clear, The concept of &quot;I am the sparrow&quot; and the concept &quot;I am the master of a myriad of shapes&quot; have some inherent conflict. I'm hoping that there are ways to do something moderately close to either archetype, or to choose from several middle paths between these two. Because Lunars are a real part of the setting that is described and not some Hero system like entity whose abilities are defined entirely by the player I wouldn't expect to see either &quot;extreme&quot; but I'm hoping that increased xp expenditure won't force me towards one or the other. In previous editions I think that a lack of ways to expand upon the spirit shape lead to characters with character sheets filled with non-spirit shape options which in turn lead to de-emphasized importance of the spirit shape.<br /> <br /> If I start with the concept of the sparrow Lunar (or what have you) I want to have a worthwhile selection of ways to be thematically focused on my sparrow (or whatever) nature. There are lots of ways to do this. <br /> <br /> But some of them are clearly not the way that 3rd ed is taking Lunars. <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Spirit shape specific charms that do things that grant the Exalt's spirit shape advantages aren't going to be there. Certainly they'll be charms that can augment the spirit shape, but they would also work with any other shape. <br /> <br /> Being able to spend xp to increase the physical attributes of the spirit shape or allow for increases in the characters attributes to be reflected as increases in the spirit shape's attributes don't look to be options that will be covered.</div> <br /> <br /> Edit: It's not as if I played that much 2nd ed. Lunars ( I haven't touched them since 1rst ed.). It was just a passing thought. It probably isn't worth the effort that folks are putting in to this discussion. We'll get some Lunars, they'll be as they'll be and we'll react to them then, and none of these thoughts will matter. <br /> <br /> Discussing the importance of the spirit shape at this point is only for amusement. It is too late to change things and I, at least, don't know what the new Lunars will be yet. By setting vague expectations that may well not come to pass I run the risk of not seeing value in the new version because they fail to meet some irrelevant set of weird expectations I have for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T12:20:08-07:00","id":1249190,"title":"","content":"Are you talking about 'The Sparrow' as in &quot;I'm Batman&quot; or as something else here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T12:28:30-07:00","id":1249192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249190#post1249190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you talking about 'The Sparrow' as in &quot;I'm Batman&quot; or as something else here?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm talking about having abilities associated with one's spirit shape. Batman is something that I don't want. He's a guy dressed as a bat but otherwise his schtick isn't batlike at all. The sparrow lunar should be able to change in a super sparrow who has supernaturally great speed, strength, and toughness, or who has a chirp of unequalled beauty that can melt hearts, or who can craft nests that can protect, trap, or heal. I want some options for a non-trivial portion of the lunar's powers to be associated with their spirit shape.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T12:58:34-07:00","id":1249198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249192#post1249192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm talking about having abilities associated with one's spirit shape. Batman is something that I don't want. He's a guy dressed as a bat but otherwise his schtick isn't batlike at all. The sparrow lunar should be able to change in a super sparrow who has supernaturally great speed, strength, and toughness, or who has a chirp of unequalled beauty that can melt hearts, or who can craft nests that can protect, trap, or heal. I want some options for a non-trivial portion of the lunar's powers to be associated with their spirit shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have missed something, but it sounded like only partial shapeshifting/bodily feature Charms were getting the totemic tag. So a Lunar Batman would have an alternate path for getting patagia and sonar, but not being The Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T13:51:27-07:00","id":1249211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249198#post1249198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may have missed something, but it sounded like only partial shapeshifting/bodily feature Charms were getting the totemic tag. So a Lunar Batman would have an alternate path for getting patagia and sonar, but not being The Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not the case. For example, a lot of warfare Charms, none of which are in physical Attributes, have Totemic access by way of various physical Attributes for Lunars whose spirit shapes are pack hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T13:56:35-07:00","id":1249213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249211#post1249211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not the case. For example, a lot of warfare Charms, none of which are in physical Attributes, have Totemic access by way of various physical Attributes for Lunars whose spirit shapes are pack hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, what if the beast normally hunts in packs but the parameters of the totem lead to a totemic expression like a &quot;lone wolf&quot; archetype?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T14:45:02-07:00","id":1249216,"title":"","content":"That would be an individual thing, surely?<br /> <br /> Wolves hunt in packs, so they get warfare charms as physical. A lone wolf just... doesn't take those charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T15:06:32-07:00","id":1249222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249192#post1249192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm talking about having abilities associated with one's spirit shape. Batman is something that I don't want. He's a guy dressed as a bat but otherwise his schtick isn't batlike at all. The sparrow lunar should be able to change in a super sparrow who has supernaturally great speed, strength, and toughness, or who has a chirp of unequalled beauty that can melt hearts, or who can craft nests that can protect, trap, or heal. I want some options for a non-trivial portion of the lunar's powers to be associated with their spirit shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would approach that from the direction of a Lunar's character, as revealed by spirit shape, and an assumption that their Charm selections are discerning.<br /> <br /> If you have a spirit shape of a sparrow, I would expect you to have a personality inclined to things like powers for enchanting singing and speedy hunting. Some of them may even be Protean, and better when in your preferred bird shape.<br /> <br /> I say this as an attempt to find a compromise for what you want in what I see as coming up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T15:09:21-07:00","id":1249224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249213#post1249213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, what if the beast normally hunts in packs but the parameters of the totem lead to a totemic expression like a &quot;lone wolf&quot; archetype?</div> </div> </div> </div>To minimize ambiguity and confusion, all Totemic criteria are strictly objective things. An animal is either part of a species that hunts in packs, or it isn't. An animal is either poisonous/venomous, or it isn't. There's nothing like &quot;animals associated with death&quot; or &quot;animals that look cute.&quot; If a particular route of Totemic access doesn't fit the cultural symbolism your character attributes to their spirit shape, they can simply not take those Charms, or just learn them as Charms of the Attribute they belong to normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T17:47:57-07:00","id":1249238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249216#post1249216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be an individual thing, surely?<br /> <br /> Wolves hunt in packs, so they get warfare charms as physical. A lone wolf just... doesn't take those charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also exactly how you can make your Totem as important to your character as you want it to be.<br /> <br /> If you choose an elephant totem, you can choose to favor Strength and/or Stamina, but nothing forces you to do both. Nothing forces you to ignore Dexterity, either; you can get that or not, depending on how strongly you want to stick to &quot;elephant&quot;. You might not even be obligated to learn the Towering Beast Shape Charm that would let you actually turn into an elephant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T20:15:29-07:00","id":1249259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249224#post1249224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To minimize ambiguity and confusion, all Totemic criteria are strictly objective things. An animal is either part of a species that hunts in packs, or it isn't. An animal is either poisonous/venomous, or it isn't. There's nothing like &quot;animals associated with death&quot; or &quot;animals that look cute.&quot; If a particular route of Totemic access doesn't fit the cultural symbolism your character attributes to their spirit shape, they can simply not take those Charms, or just learn them as Charms of the Attribute they belong to normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Lunar's player and storyteller agree that, say, Fox Totems should have Totemic access to hypnosis charms or something, is that sort of thing likely to break the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T05:40:41-07:00","id":1249340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249259#post1249259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Lunar's player and storyteller agree that, say, Fox Totems should have Totemic access to hypnosis charms or something, is that sort of thing likely to break the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would it? All Totemic does is change the Attribute prerequisite of a Charm. I can't imagine that unbalancing anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T07:39:51-07:00","id":1249405,"title":"","content":"Edit: Sorry, wrong thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-28-2018, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T05:46:07-07:00","id":1249676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249169#post1249169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Spirit shape specific charms that do things that grant the Exalt's spirit shape advantages aren't going to be there. Certainly they'll be charms that can augment the spirit shape, but they would also work with any other shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the availability of Charms thematic to your spirit shape in other shapes detracts from the focus on your spirit shape. Quite the opposite. Your spirit shape is part of your nature, always, and your Charms reflect that nature. Your spirit shape is one of the central pillars of your identity - maybe not the only factor that might inspire Charm choices, but presumably you chose that animal because you wanted to explore its themes, so it's going to influence a big chunk of your Charm choices. In this way, your spirit shape is reflected in your capabilities no matter what shape the situation calls for you to be in. <br /> <br /> You can sing a song so beautiful it melts hearts because you have the nature of a songbird, and when you're in the form of a bear that bear can sing a song that melts hearts <i>because it's actually a sparrow-souled moon-marked demigod disguised as a bear</i>. Your bull-totem Lunar can headbutt people into next week even in fluffy bunny form <i>because his heart carries the strength of the bull, always</i>. The honey-tongued courtesan seeps venom from her perfect smile <i>because no matter what form she wears, she is a poisonous snake</i>. These Charms are always with you because they reflect who you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T11:14:32-07:00","id":1249999,"title":"","content":"It occurred to me that one benefit of the Totem keyword is that it would allow diversifying builds and maintaining fidelity in character concepts even within a Caste that some Charms might be natural to, without letting the limit on your Caste Attributes be a problem.<br /> <br /> ...Yeah, I don't get it either. Let me provide a concrete example.<br /> <br /> Take a Full Moon Caste with the spirit shape of, say, a hornet. It makes sense for such a character to have the poison Charms, right? And good news, Stamina is a Full Moon Caste Attribute, so no worries.<br /> <br /> But the player also wants Strength and Dexterity, so one of the three is going to have to count as a Favoured Attribute. And when they think about the character, it really makes sense as somebody who would have a couple of non-Full Moon Attributes Favoured, and when they look over the list they think that really, poison stuff is <i>all</i> that they want from Stamina. So they get to go with Wits and one other non-physical Attribute, and it all works out.<br /> <br /> I'm personally interested in seeing what alternative Attributes might be given for certain Strength Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T11:50:58-07:00","id":1250016,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you can apply DBT\u2019s boosts to animal forms, or if that would be \u201cunbalanced\u201d in combination with the Protean effects of other Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T12:09:59-07:00","id":1250024,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it specifically only works if you're in hybrid form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T15:40:00-07:00","id":1250089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1248119-will-lunars-have-clear-ways-to-keep-the-spirit-shape-of-central-importance?p=1249676#post1249676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can sing a song so beautiful it melts hearts because you have the nature of a songbird, and when you're in the form of a bear that bear can sing a song that melts hearts <i>because it's actually a sparrow-souled moon-marked demigod disguised as a bear</i>. Your bull-totem Lunar can headbutt people into next week even in fluffy bunny form <i>because his heart carries the strength of the bull, always</i>. The honey-tongued courtesan seeps venom from her perfect smile <i>because no matter what form she wears, she is a poisonous snake</i>. These Charms are always with you because they reflect who you are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually not sure if all of those examples will work...<br /> <br /> EDIT: And even if it did, I presume that one's songbird totem Lunar would be able to have the strength of a bear in their spirit shape, so what does that say about things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 08-30-2018, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}